### What is this question really testing?

Bias for action balanced with collaboration. Pure heroics that bypass owners can damage trust. The ideal is stepping in because the business needs it, then looping in the owners so the fix sticks.

```java
package com.bank.interview;
public class OwnershipTest {
    enum Signal { PROACTIVE, PASSIVE }
    public static Signal evaluate(boolean actedOnBusiness, boolean loopedInOwner) {
        return (actedOnBusiness && loopedInOwner) ? Signal.PROACTIVE : Signal.PASSIVE;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(evaluate(true, true)); // PROACTIVE
    }
}
```

### What was the problem nobody owned?

The nightly reconciliation job at National Bank of India had been silently failing for several nights. Nobody was confirming that customer balances matched the ledger.

```java
package com.bank.service;
import java.util.logging.Logger;
public class SilentFailure {
    private static final Logger log = Logger.getLogger(SilentFailure.class.getName());
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        log.warning("Reconciliation job: last success = 4 days ago");
        log.warning("Risk: ledger and balances may have drifted");
        log.info("This belongs to another team, but the risk is too high to ignore");
    }
}
```

### How did you contain the immediate risk?

Confirmed current balances were still correct, then reached out to the owning team with exact evidence.

```java
package com.bank.service;
public class ContainAndCoordinate {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Step 1: Verified current balances match ledger (no drift yet)");
        System.out.println("Step 2: Sent owning team the log evidence of 4-day failure");
        System.out.println("Step 3: Did NOT silently take over their system");
    }
}
```

### How did you build a durable monitor?

A freshness monitor records the last successful run and alerts if the job goes too long without succeeding.

```java
package com.bank.service;
import java.time.Duration;
import java.time.Instant;
import java.util.logging.Logger;
public class FreshnessMonitor {
    private static final Logger log = Logger.getLogger(FreshnessMonitor.class.getName());
    private static final Duration MAX_ALLOWED_GAP = Duration.ofHours(26);
    public static void check(Instant lastSuccess) {
        Duration gap = Duration.between(lastSuccess, Instant.now());
        if (gap.compareTo(MAX_ALLOWED_GAP) > 0) {
            log.severe("ALERT: Reconciliation stale by " + gap.toHours() + " hours");
        } else {
            log.info("Reconciliation fresh: last success " + gap.toHours() + "h ago");
        }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        check(Instant.now().minus(Duration.ofHours(100))); // simulating stale
    }
}
```

```text
ALERT: Reconciliation stale by 100 hours
```

### Why did you step in instead of letting it go?

The potential impact was financial and regulatory. If balances and the ledger drift apart unnoticed, real problems follow.

```java
package com.bank.interview;
public class WhyStepIn {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Impact if ignored: balance drift -> financial + regulatory risk");
        System.out.println("Cost of stepping in: 2 hours of my time");
        System.out.println("Judgment: the business impact far outweighs the effort");
    }
}
```

### How did you hand back to the real owner?

Gave the owning team the evidence, the immediate verification, and the freshness monitor so they could maintain it going forward.

```java
package com.bank.interview;
public class HandBack {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Handed to owning team:");
        System.out.println("  1. Log evidence of 4-day failure");
        System.out.println("  2. Verification that balances are currently correct");
        System.out.println("  3. Freshness monitor code + alert configuration");
        System.out.println("They own it; I enabled them, not replaced them.");
    }
}
```

### What was the lasting impact?

Silent failures of this class became impossible to miss because the freshness monitor pages the right team automatically.

```java
package com.bank.interview;
public class OwnershipResult {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Before: silent failure went unnoticed for days");
        System.out.println("After: automatic alert within 26 hours of missed run");
        System.out.println("Ownership: real team maintains it; I built the safety net");
    }
}
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

```java
package com.bank.interview;
public class OwnershipFollowUps {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Team annoyed? -> No, grateful for the evidence and the monitor");
        System.out.println("Would you do it again? -> Yes, whenever the business risk justifies it");
        System.out.println("How often do you step out of scope? -> Only when impact is high and owners are unaware");
    }
}
```
